19th September 1965\
My dear Mr.Woolf, \
It has taken days for me to recover from the wonderful surprise of your gift to me last Wednesday and even now I can hardly believe it is true. I can never thank you enough for all your kindness and generosity over the years I have worked for you and please do always let me know if there is anything more I can do at any time. \
I have worked very hard since George died to enable me to keep my flat and and meet all the expenses involved and the car has certainly helped to make life easier for me even though I have only had it for a week. \
Again expressing my very grateful thanks. \
Yours very sincerely, \
Constance A. Edwards}